OK   IMPORTANCE: an owner with higher importance BLOCKS pressure (BLOCKED_BY_STRONGER_OWNER) -- explicit user value outranks temporal pressure
OK   DEADLINE TODAY: an owner with its deadline today BLOCKS pressure even against a higher-importance loser
OK   DEADLINE: with deadline-today and importance tied, an owner with a stronger (present / earlier) deadline BLOCKS pressure
OK   a WEAKER owner on a stronger dimension (the loser outranks it) is a PRECEDENCE_ANOMALY -- classified explicitly, never silently called eligibility
OK   ORIGINALORDER-ONLY DIFFERENCE: owners and loser that tie on every stronger dimension are eligible however originalOrder would order them (it is weaker than pressure and is not part of the facts)
=== owners: 0..N, deduplicated, historical vs final, all-owner rule ===
OK   MULTI-OWNER ALL-TIE: two final owners, both tie above pressure -> eligible against ALL final owners; the observation carries both owners (cardinality 2, never collapsed to one)
OK   MULTI-OWNER MIXED: one owner ties, the other has HIGHER importance -> BLOCKED_BY_STRONGER_OWNER (not globally eligible); per-owner comparisons AND the aggregate are both recorded
OK   an anomaly is never hidden by another owner's block: a loser-stronger owner plus an owner-stronger owner is PRECEDENCE_ANOMALY
OK   MULTIPLE EVENTS, SAME OWNER (three attempted intervals, two rounds): the owner is compared ONCE; the event count (3) is metadata only, never strength
OK   HISTORICAL OWNER REMOVED: A1 (stronger, but no longer Proposed) keeps its comparison as evidence yet does NOT block; the remaining FINAL owner A2 ties -> eligible against all FINAL owners
OK   OWNER NOT IN THE FINAL RESULT AT ALL is valid history, not corruption: it is NOT_FINAL_PROPOSED and (no final owner remains) the classification is NO_FINAL_CONTENTION_OWNER
OK   only the loser's OWN contention relationships are used: an unrelated Proposed candidate never enters the owner set
